    {
      "id": "a28863a0-a4b7-47f0-8fd4-9918b3b72b1e",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1328,
        -256
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 720,
        "height": 832,
        "content": "## Clean Plate Tracker for Kids\n\nTurn the daily \"please finish your food\" struggle into a game. A parent sends a photo of the plate after a meal to a LINE bot, Google Gemini judges how much was eaten, and the child gets a cheerful message with a stamp card that fills up over time.\n\nWho's it for: parents of young children who eat slowly, leave food behind, or need a little motivation at the table.\n\n### How it works\n1. A photo sent to your LINE bot triggers the workflow.\n2. The image is downloaded from the LINE Messaging API.\n3. Google Gemini scores how much of the meal was eaten (0-100) and writes a short, always-kind message for the child.\n4. Past records are read from Google Sheets to count total stamps and the current daily streak.\n5. Today's result is appended to the sheet.\n6. The child receives the praise, a stamp card and how many stamps are left until the next reward.\n\n### Setup\n1. Create a LINE Messaging API channel and copy the Channel access token.\n2. Put the token, your Google Sheets ID and your child's name into the Config node.\n3. Copy the Webhook URL into the LINE Developers console.\n4. Prepare a sheet with the columns: Date, Time, Child Name, Clean Plate, Score, Leftovers, Stamps Earned, Comment.\n\n### Customization tips\n- CLEAN_PLATE_THRESHOLD makes the judge stricter or gentler.\n- STAMPS_PER_REWARD sets how many stamps earn a reward.\n- Only the plate needs to be in the photo. No faces required."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
